// Generated by tools/st_gen_params.py; do not edit.
//
// The network runs at 320x240 internally: 15 DDR passes
// (15 including pre), 29 conv layers, 5 adds.  See docs/st-accel-engine-adr.md.
//
// The requant ROM holds one word per output channel of every conv layer in
// manifest order, then one word per add; ST_ADD_RQ_BASE is the first add word.
//
// The tables are function lookups with case statements, not localparam arrays:
// Efinity does not accept arrays of structs as parameters.
//
//   st_layer(i)     layer i in manifest order: kind, channels, ROM bases, clamp
//   st_pass(i)      pass i; pass 0 is pre, pass i is PASSES[i-1] of st_golden.py
//   st_region(pt)   DDR region of point pt; all-zero for a non-DDR point
//   st_region_point(i) i-th point that has a DDR region, for iteration
//
// lo/hi are 10-bit two's complement: relu 0..127, none -127..127, head 0..255.
// in_w/in_h of a pass describe the grid the engine works on; with upsample set
// the main DDR source region is in_w/2 x in_h/2 (see st_region).
